<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32883" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ōrātrix</span></b> ,
		īcis, f.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>She that prays</i> or <i>beseeches</i>, <i>a female suppliant</i> (rare but
			class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">me oratricem haud sprevisti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Mil. 4, 2, 80</span></i>
			: pacis et foederis, * <i><span class="en">Cic. Rep.
				2, 8, 14</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> A transl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥητορική</span>,
				<i>rhetoric</i>, <i>oratory</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Quint. 2, 14, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
